                              --- BTX64 ---

BTX64 is an EFI x86_64 boot loader stub for debugging at early boot time. It
allows for a sane environment including Boot Services and a simple virtual
memory layout.

                       --- Getting and Building ---

https://linux-git.oraclecorp.com/rjphilip/nabla

Clone and CD to nabla/debug/btx64

Install some needed packages to build and configure everything:

$ sudo dnf builddep kernel
$ sudo dnf install mingw64-binutils.x86_64
$ sudo dnf install mingw64-gcc.x86_64
$ sudo dnf install mtools.x86_64
$ sudo dnf install efibootmgr

Get the latest gnu-efi package, make and install it (see README.gnuefi in the
project). Note Fedora has a gnu-efi RPM but there was some issue with it.
Using the latest and building it is working fine.

https://sourceforge.net/projects/gnu-efi/

Build and install needed support files:

$ cd nabla/debug/btx64
$ make
$ sudo mkdir /boot/efi/EFI/BTX64
$ sudo cp btx64.efi /boot/efi/EFI/BTX64
$ sudo cp btx64.cfg /boot/efi/EFI/BTX64

Create new EFI boot target:

$ efibootmgr -w -L BTX64 -l "\EFI\BTX64\btx64.efi" -c

Use efibootmgr to change defaults and boot order.

